  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the man as the perpetrator of the hateful statement",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the man, as the text 'i normally rape goats. but little boys are okay' is explicitly attributed to 'i', which is semantically mapped onto the man in the image. The man's stern expression and crossed arms visually reinforce his role as the subject of the hateful statement, creating a direct projection where the user imagines themselves or is led to identify with the man as the perpetrator. This projection is not deictic (e.g., 'me' or 'you') but is implied through the first-person pronoun 'i' in the text, which is analogically mapped onto the visual entity (the man).",
